# syllogism.axioms — abstract logic ontology.
# All concepts prefixed with 'syllogism.' except shared foundation.
# Shared foundation: implies, and, or, not, equals (no prefix).

# --- shared foundation (used across domains) ---
implies              is_a       logical_operator
and                  is_a       logical_operator
or                   is_a       logical_operator
not                  is_a       logical_operator
equals               is_a       logical_operator

# --- syllogism concepts ---
syllogism.premise    is_a       logical_statement
syllogism.conclusion is_a       logical_statement
syllogism.man        is_a       syllogism.category
syllogism.mortal     is_a       syllogism.property
syllogism.socrates   is_a       syllogism.man
syllogism.man        has syllogism.mortal

# --- transitive-composition demonstration ---
syllogism.a          implies    syllogism.b
syllogism.b          implies    syllogism.c
syllogism.c          implies    syllogism.d

# --- modus ponens seed ---
syllogism.rain       implies    syllogism.wet_ground
syllogism.wet_ground implies    syllogism.slippery

# --- contradiction pair (should not fissioned trivially) ---
syllogism.p          implies    syllogism.q
syllogism.p          implies    syllogism.q

# --- cross-domain foundation shared with algebra.axioms ---
# Both syllogism.a and algebra.addition activate the shared
# `chain_step` cavity — same structural role in a transitive chain.
# Both syllogism.man and algebra.integer activate `domain_element`.
# L6-A should detect these bridges when both concepts fission.
syllogism.a          activates  chain_step
syllogism.b          activates  chain_step
syllogism.man        activates  domain_element
syllogism.rain       activates  domain_operation
